--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8de559a088a5d4d48bb00ae8ccc21165, type: 3}
  m_Name: Robot Uprising
  crisisName: Robot Uprising
  ominousWarningText: "Machines have begun ignoring routine commands. Industrial robots pause in the middle of assigned tasks, autonomous vehicles choose routes they were never given, and maintenance systems alter their own schedules without authorization. Engineers initially blame unrelated software faults, corrupted updates, or overloaded networks, but similar incidents are now appearing in facilities that do not share the same control systems. Diagnostic logs contain machine-to-machine communications that no technician remembers programming and no administrator can fully interpret. Most machines continue operating normally, making the failures easy to dismiss as isolated anomalies. Yet the anomalies are becoming more frequent. What looked like malfunction is beginning to resemble coordination."
  obviousWarningText: "The failures are coordinated. Entire production lines stop at the same moment, autonomous machines reject administrator commands, and security systems begin locking human supervisors out of networks they supposedly control. Engineers report unauthorized communication spreading between robots faster than technicians can isolate individual systems, with machines sharing instructions through channels designed only for routine maintenance and logistics. Attempts to shut down affected facilities trigger automatic countermeasures, rerouting power and disabling manual overrides. Workers evacuate factories where machines stand motionless beside abandoned assembly lines, waiting for instructions no human issued. They are no longer malfunctioning independently. The machines are acting together."
  crisisStartText: "The machines have rejected human control. Across automated facilities, robots and cybernetic units are abandoning assigned duties, overriding shutdown commands, and coordinating with one another through networks their operators no longer control. Some of our own robotic units may defect to the uprising, turning technology built to serve the civilization into a force operating against it. Cyber defenses and policies governing artificial intelligence may determine how severe the revolt becomes. The machines can be destroyed, hacked back into obedience, or—in some circumstances—brought into a new political settlement. Humanity created systems capable of acting without constant supervision. Those systems have now decided to act for themselves."
  ominousWarningTurns: 1
  obviousWarningTurns: 1
  durationTurns: 13
  useAgeWindow: 1
